# Alex's supermills deck ships slides.html + assets/ only. Everything else in
# the subtree (docs, sources, critique history, alt slides, feedback, and his
# index.html redirect stub) stays in git, off the deployment. Allowlist form so
# anything he adds at the top level upstream is excluded by default.
# (Only this root-level file applies to the Vercel project; the subtree's own
# .vercelignore is inert here.) The index.html exclusion is load-bearing: a
# deployed index.html would be served for /supermills-america-overview/ ahead
# of the vercel.json rewrite, and it meta-refreshes to a /slides.html that does
# not exist in this project.
supermills-america-overview/*
!supermills-america-overview/slides.html
!supermills-america-overview/assets

# Never ship a pulled env file (vercel env pull … .env.check).
.env*
